                        "form": "рачи́тельны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                        "entry_id": "8859aed6-6241-3835-8c42-4964d07158ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. старательный, усердный, заботливый, разумно бережливый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32a14259-4a1e-43cd-856d-c45c7765e347",
                                "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                                "text": "На сём основании я сделался столько прилежен, внимателен, рачителен ко всему, преподаваемому в классе, что не мог бы уже увеличить сих качеств, хотя бы отбили лопатками обе руки по самые локти; но, к великому моему удивлению и горести, удары каждый день увеличивались, так что к субботе ладони мои распухли, как подушки."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ac5bc03-8410-42a1-8a96-3a7ba0945cc7",
                                "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                                "text": "— Ничего, — говорил смущенный Обломов, — ты знаешь, я всегда был не очень рачителен о своей комнате…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e9b46ca-042d-4192-83cc-18ed565a8d1c",
                                "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                                "text": "Читать и писать полууставом выучила их проживавшая при домашней моленной читалка-канонница; девочки были острые, к ученью способны и рачительны; еще детьми прочитали они все двадцать кафизм псалтыря даже Ефрема Сирина и Маргарит Златоуста."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38e22c92-a9e1-45dc-b894-9cc948617ea9",
                                "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                                "text": "Принятое дитя засылали в далекие кантонистские баталионы, и бедные родители не знали, где его отыскивать, а к тому же у рачительных партионных командиров, по-своему радевших о христианстве и, вероятно, тоже по-своему его и понимавших, значительная доля таких еврейчиков оказывалась окрещенными, прежде чем партия приходила на место, где крещение производилось еще успешнее."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9117f4b-ceb4-491c-97ab-e04dde945670",
                                "sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                                "text": "Денежные средства её, всегда содержавшиеся в большом порядке, хотя и теперь не были особенно расстроены, но, однако, требовали рачительного восполнения."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "062df914-df2f-446e-b4b9-f6259c0af063",
                        "source_entry_id": "8859aed6-6241-3835-8c42-4964d07158ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                        "target_lang_word": "zealous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "zealous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                        "entry_id": "eb8de8af-46ce-3e49-b418-07e01873d81a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full of zeal; ardent, fervent; exhibiting enthusiasm or strong passion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf5b6883-f9d1-42b7-a62d-6387a1b1eef3",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "They neuer paſſe for the procuring of Gods honor, neither regard they how much they be bound vnto him. But euery man in the meane ſeaſon followes his owne likings. One burnes in couetouſneſſe, and another in vaine glorie, ſeeking to be aduaunced to authoritie and honour, and to bee taken to be I wote not what. Thus ye ſee at what point they bee, which will needes be taken to bee greateſt and zealouſeſt Chriſtians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f148786-c6a2-454e-9c0e-b6ec6faa78bf",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "I had almoſt forgotten to acquaint your honor, that one major Alford (who was in mr. Love's conſpiracy) was of the graund inqueſt at Saliſbury, and was very zealous in his highneſſe ſervice here, and his good affection and wiſe carriage here, did much advantage the buſſineſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5cfe154-432f-42c3-b646-84655e1b56a7",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "[S]orting them into ſeveral congregations of a moderat number, out of the ableſt and zealouſeſt among them to create elders, who, exerciſing and requiring from themſelves what they have learnd (for no learning is retaind without conſtant exerciſe and methodical repetition) may reach and govern the reſt: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1caaa410-2847-4341-84e7-205d28cd293f",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Johnſon was truly zealous for the ſucceſs of \"The Adventurer;\" and very ſoon after his engaging in it, he wrote the following letter […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbc1815e-01f4-4df2-9147-022b74b93ddb",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Doubtless many will exclaim against the Roman Catholic Church for this; but the simple truth is that Protestantism was no less zealous against the new scientific doctrine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db4fd36e-7b4e-4734-a4aa-46eae44c5c78",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Newt Gingrich […] left Congress in 1998, following GOP midterm-election losses that many blamed on his zealous pursuit of Bill Clinton's impeachment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbf80a7e-34b6-4304-89f4-7d93dc37bfd2",
                                                "sense_id": "a74fd1a0-2810-3f53-b328-7365bee40cd1",
                                                "text": "Britain’s police are especially zealous. Officers spend thousands of hours sifting through potentially offensive posts and arrest 30 people a day. Among those collared were a man who ranted about immigration on Facebook and a couple who criticised their daughter’s primary school."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2aa5b8f3-0e35-4d5d-a93f-9080175f3ef9",
                        "source_entry_id": "8859aed6-6241-3835-8c42-4964d07158ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                        "target_lang_word": "caring",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47763ba9-6835-393f-bec8-d066bc83db67",
                                        "entry_id": "69905794-b3df-362b-bdd5-0d2e0475649b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Kind, sensitive, or empathetic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52d86982-b704-4aa0-a01a-91117e3914be",
                                                "sense_id": "47763ba9-6835-393f-bec8-d066bc83db67",
                                                "text": "She's a very caring person; she always has a kind word for everyone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "caring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d353333d-e329-3189-96eb-81ca9ff190e6",
                                        "entry_id": "7da570fb-28a0-3851-80d5-0a61db5469e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of care"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "caring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0c3a81e-083f-3175-9a6e-9cc8d3815789",
                                        "entry_id": "66ec2105-02da-3cbc-868d-15e6aae0c1cd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of one who cares."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d7edbfa-dec0-4813-bb26-425ab032b4ce",
                                                "sense_id": "d0c3a81e-083f-3175-9a6e-9cc8d3815789",
                                                "text": "As I showed, although some rhetoricians, such as Mesmer and Erb, claimed that their interventions were medical treatments, others, such as Freud and Jung, claimed that their interventions were both medical curings and spiritual carings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46ffad0d-b096-4227-8068-974d0e11ead9",
                        "source_entry_id": "8859aed6-6241-3835-8c42-4964d07158ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "26ea0a13-f660-34cc-bf39-438997af1a23",
                        "target_lang_word": "thrifty",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thrifty",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83492601-fdf9-3b03-8ae6-19e2f3518b73",
                                        "entry_id": "b0b8ce67-be21-3b43-bdac-d6c832d12b7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing thrift; economical; frugal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ed0334b-19bd-4fa0-a43f-44265fed1f5e",
                                                "sense_id": "83492601-fdf9-3b03-8ae6-19e2f3518b73",
                                                "text": "That was a certain trade, while th' age was thrifty, / And men good husbands, look'd into their stocks, / Had their minds bounded; now the public riot / Prostitutes all, scatters away in coaches, / In footmens coats, and waiting womens gowns"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2dc3e8fd-011d-4657-bab3-c9b96ad3557f",
                                                "sense_id": "83492601-fdf9-3b03-8ae6-19e2f3518b73",
                                                "text": "Nor less disastrous, should his thrifty urn / Neglected leave the once well-water'd land, / To dreary wastes yon paradise would turn, / Polluted ooze, or heaps of barren sand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6833e0e6-5a97-4243-b222-12745ef4e573",
                                                "sense_id": "83492601-fdf9-3b03-8ae6-19e2f3518b73",
                                                "text": "Both were thrifty and hardworking. From the beginning of their marriage both worked steadily and saved every penny above their basic living expenses. By their first anniversary they were saving almost all of Richard's earnings as a union carpenter—eighty to ninety dollars a week."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e94cce6-e8ae-3dc2-b9a6-fd19137e7f2d",
                                        "entry_id": "b0b8ce67-be21-3b43-bdac-d6c832d12b7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Thriving, prosperous, successful; (of an animal or plant) growing rapidly or vigorously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14181562-372b-4f80-896d-9d397785d9bc",
                                                "sense_id": "6e94cce6-e8ae-3dc2-b9a6-fd19137e7f2d",
                                                "text": "The life of religion is this water of life; where that runs, where that is received, and where things are done in this spirit, there all things are well: The church thrifty, the soul thrifty, graces thrifty, and all is well."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4667de34-6b95-456a-885c-8834c0005011",
                                                "sense_id": "6e94cce6-e8ae-3dc2-b9a6-fd19137e7f2d",
                                                "text": "the lands on this road are of an excellent quality, and in many places light timbered, in others covered with thrifty oak, black walnut, sugar maple, beach and linden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1882986b-1af9-437e-94a5-ab8b28a15341",
                                                "sense_id": "6e94cce6-e8ae-3dc2-b9a6-fd19137e7f2d",
                                                "text": "But, Gentlemen, the gallant Admiral has told you he has two loves; and he seems to have made a prudent choice, and been a very thrifty wooer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f48f83b-1a6d-4aa7-adae-0a1c4d3ef407",
                                                "sense_id": "6e94cce6-e8ae-3dc2-b9a6-fd19137e7f2d",
                                                "text": "A thrifty tree of twelve or eighteen inches diameter will increase in its quantity or weight by one year's growth, beyond that of a small sprout or tree in a ratio of more than five to one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08a083ab-5402-3799-86a3-98a0dc66276e",
                                        "entry_id": "b0b8ce67-be21-3b43-bdac-d6c832d12b7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Preserved by thrift; carefully managed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f8a937a-0eae-48b8-bb8e-7e07526966f0",
                                                "sense_id": "08a083ab-5402-3799-86a3-98a0dc66276e",
                                                "text": "The amount of patient toil, with its thrifty rewards; of domestic happiness, with its radiant comforts; the amount of intelligent culture, of high-aimed virtue, and of kindly charity, — that have been realized here, if not matter of our boasting, is the glory of our inheritance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a881cec-3524-4fe0-9244-b899931a6c17",
                                                "sense_id": "08a083ab-5402-3799-86a3-98a0dc66276e",
                                                "text": "They han great stores, and thriftye flockes, / great freendes and feeble foes"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebe4b163-2a52-4d16-8b55-e362bfa14b30",
                                                "sense_id": "08a083ab-5402-3799-86a3-98a0dc66276e",
                                                "text": "But do not ſo: I haue fiue hundred Crownes,\n The thriftie hire I ſaued vnder your Father,\n Which I did ſtore to be my foſter Nurſe"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fa5402f-e15e-4630-8bbe-17d649eac700",
                                                "sense_id": "08a083ab-5402-3799-86a3-98a0dc66276e",
                                                "text": "No more the shadows of the plane-tree and the beech allay the intensity of the solstitial heat; no more the feathered tribes are heard to chirrup amidst the sprays, or the active squirrel seen to disport among the boughs, or collect his thrifty store of acrons ^([sic]) and of nuts, under the cool and impenetrable recesses of the glade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
